    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite ran green (17 tests, `BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `Cp09Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` assignment on owner creation, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, assign the code just before persisting via a new `generateCustomerCode(lastName)` helper:\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (`Math.min(3, \u2026)` guards short names).\n   - `NNNN` = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits with `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", \u2026)`. Computing it before the save means the count excludes the new owner, satisfying \"one more than the current number of owners.\"\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it (MapStruct auto-maps the same-named entity field into the response).\n\n4. **`resources/db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added a `customer_code` column to the `owners` table (the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none` with hsqldb, so the DDL is required).\n\nThe test confirms both the format (`SMI-`, `JON-` prefixes) and that the global sequence increments by one across successive creates.",
